# Scenarios that are LIVE — implemented, and required to be green.
# Everything else carries @planned. A milestone's change moves lines INTO this file.
# Format: <feature file>::<scenario name>

01_form_detection.feature::content magic disambiguates a shared extension
01_form_detection.feature::.rs is reserved for tile-rs unconditionally
01_form_detection.feature::an unrecognisable file is refused with the candidate forms named
01_form_detection.feature::-f overrides both magic and extension
01_form_detection.feature::a form claimed by -f that contradicts strong magic is warned about, not silently accepted

02_transform_dispatch.feature::the reader/writer matrix is one command away
02_transform_dispatch.feature::same-form optimization names the missing reader, in the right tense
02_transform_dispatch.feature::a target absent from THIS build is a different answer from one nobody wrote
02_transform_dispatch.feature::same-form optimization exists only for the forms tile-rs owns
02_transform_dispatch.feature::a lift does not silently compose into a lowering route
02_transform_dispatch.feature::the composed route runs when it is named explicitly
02_transform_dispatch.feature::with no reader for the input form, a lift says which work is missing
02_transform_dispatch.feature::every route reports a fidelity class, and says where it was measured

04_profile_and_optimize.feature::-i and -o together are a usage error, not a silent precedence rule
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::bare -O means -O2
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::an unmeasured architecture makes the profile refuse, not guess
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::the 950 SKUs refuse bounds and invent no core count
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::a target with genuinely no such limit answers Ok rather than refusing
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::the profile surfaces the hazard model

05_platform_and_targets.feature::the default output target follows the detected accelerator
05_platform_and_targets.feature::an AMD GPU is not an AMD NPU

10_portability_and_grammar.feature::cfg gates are confined to the platform module
10_portability_and_grammar.feature::the documented options are accepted with both spellings
10_portability_and_grammar.feature::-v is version and -V is verbose, as specified
10_portability_and_grammar.feature::--help documents every option, its default, and its exit codes
10_portability_and_grammar.feature::exit codes are grouped by remedy, not by subsystem
10_portability_and_grammar.feature::exit 3 never claims that something is impossible
10_portability_and_grammar.feature::no C or C++ is compiled to build the tool

11_io_edges.feature::stdin with no -f is a usage error, because there is no name to sniff from
11_io_edges.feature::several inputs with a single -o is a usage error
11_io_edges.feature::a form that exists but is not compiled into this build says so

# M2 — the emitters are wired in, so the program's own behaviour is checkable
11_io_edges.feature::"-o -" writes the result to stdout and nothing else does
11_io_edges.feature::an empty input is refused, matching the emitters' own contract
11_io_edges.feature::a non-UTF8 input is refused before sniffing
11_io_edges.feature::an output directory that does not exist is an error, not a silent mkdir

# M3 — the optimize hop is a real step, so intermediates are real
02_transform_dispatch.feature::identical forms mean optimization, not a copy
03_intermediates.feature::intermediates are removed by default
03_intermediates.feature::-k keeps every hop, named by step index and form
03_intermediates.feature::the optimize hop is a step on the route, not a claim in a report
03_intermediates.feature::-O0 has no optimize hop to keep

# M4 — provisioning: verified, user-scoped, refusing what it cannot honestly do
06_toolchains.feature::a pinned artifact is fetched, verified and installed without prompting
06_toolchains.feature::acquiring the same toolchain twice does nothing the second time
06_toolchains.feature::a corrupted download is rejected before it is unpacked
06_toolchains.feature::only the toolchain the route needs is installed
06_toolchains.feature::installs are user-scoped and never touch the system
06_toolchains.feature::a toolchain that cannot be automated is refused with the exact remedy
06_toolchains.feature::what this platform can be given is one command away
06_toolchains.feature::--no-install turns acquisition into a diagnosis
06_toolchains.feature::--offline refuses a network URL but still reads a local one

# M8 — MCP over stdio: the same core, a second rendering
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::the daemon exposes the CLI's verbs as MCP tools
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::an MCP conversion and the equivalent CLI invocation agree
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::in stdio mode all logging goes to stderr
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::agent-initiated work is bounded
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::the daemon never binds TCP without an explicit token
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::stdio is the default transport and needs no token

# M5 — two stores, one storage layer; the gate is on delivery, not on the file
07_stats_and_license.feature::an unassessed headroom is displayed as unassessed, never as zero
07_stats_and_license.feature::without a license, -s still works on local attempts and explains the gap
07_stats_and_license.feature::a missing license degrades a feature but never blocks the conversion
07_stats_and_license.feature::the corpus is unreadable without the key, not merely unlisted
07_stats_and_license.feature::a license is verified offline against an embedded public key
07_stats_and_license.feature::license status with no key installed is not a failure
07_stats_and_license.feature::an invalid license is rejected with the reason
07_stats_and_license.feature::a forged token is never reported as merely expired
07_stats_and_license.feature::writes to the local store are never license-gated
07_stats_and_license.feature::the tool never fabricates a measurement to fill a column
07_stats_and_license.feature::every stats report states how old the corpus is
07_stats_and_license.feature::the corpus is read by a pure-Rust reader, not a database binding

# M7 — the MLIR-to-MLIR rewrite layer
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::each -O level runs the passes it is permitted and no others
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::a level names what it does not do, and why
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::the rewrite layer parses and prints without changing a byte
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::a pass that separated a fusion pair reverts to the input
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::-O2 refuses a tiling the target cannot hold
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::-O2 refuses to judge a tiling on an unmeasured architecture
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::-O3 without the target's compiler degrades rather than failing

# M10a — the UI server, and M9a — the engine mapping
09_ui.feature::-u serves the view on loopback and prints its address
09_ui.feature::the listener binds loopback and nothing else
09_ui.feature::the page needs nothing from the network
09_ui.feature::kernel source cannot inject markup into the page
09_ui.feature::the UI is a view over the core, not a second implementation
09_ui.feature::a headless host prints the address rather than failing
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::-m selects the engine matching the detected accelerator
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::an engine that is not on the machine names everywhere it looked
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::a failure to provision a model never costs the kernel tools
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::the engine follows the accelerator family
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::-m outside daemon mode is a usage error

# M6 — .rs inputs, through the real codegen backend
06_toolchains.feature::a set RUSTFLAGS is refused, because it would silently disable the backend
06_toolchains.feature::the codegen path is translated from the form id, not passed through

# -r/--run: the harness, the references, and the measurements
12_run.feature::a speedup is never reported without both measurements
12_run.feature::a reported speedup names what it is measured against
12_run.feature::every timing carries its sample count and its spread
12_run.feature::the reference does not allocate inside the timed region
12_run.feature::the kernel, the reference and torch all see the same input
12_run.feature::a kernel whose operation has no reference is refused, not run
12_run.feature::a kernel using two referenceable operations is refused rather than guessed at
12_run.feature::without torch the weaker comparison is still made, and labelled
12_run.feature::three sources attribute a disagreement to the right side
12_run.feature::a kernel that matches nothing is not called an inherited error
12_run.feature::two sources cannot make the attribution three sources can
12_run.feature::a relative error near zero does not dominate the accuracy figure
12_run.feature::a non-finite mismatch is counted, not averaged away
12_run.feature::--run and --info-only together are a usage error
12_run.feature::--run and --cross together are a usage error
12_run.feature::a target with no harness says so rather than pretending
12_run.feature::uv is pinned in the manifest rather than piped from a shell
12_run.feature::the torch path needs no second command from the user

# The backlog: what tile could not do, and the rule for when to stop patching
13_backlog.feature::an entry survives being written and read back
13_backlog.feature::an entry with no workaround says so rather than leaving a blank
13_backlog.feature::each entry is its own file, so two sessions do not conflict
13_backlog.feature::a handful of unrelated gaps is healthy
13_backlog.feature::three issues in one area is a design problem, not three bugs
13_backlog.feature::a cluster is reported ahead of a raw count
13_backlog.feature::enough scattered issues eventually say stop as well
13_backlog.feature::closing issues brings the verdict back, so the rule is not a ratchet
13_backlog.feature::the listing groups by area and shows each workaround
13_backlog.feature::an empty backlog says so rather than printing a bare zero
13_backlog.feature::the exit code carries the verdict so a session can branch on it
13_backlog.feature::an unknown field in an entry is an error, not something to skip
11_io_edges.feature::"-" reads stdin, and the form must then be given
11_io_edges.feature::several inputs are converted independently, and one failure does not lose the rest
11_io_edges.feature::a directory input is refused with the glob that would have worked
11_io_edges.feature::a file containing several kernels reports all of them
11_io_edges.feature::converting a multi-kernel module emits all of them into one output
11_io_edges.feature::a symlinked input is read through, and the output is named after the link
11_io_edges.feature::an output that is a symlink is refused rather than written through
05_platform_and_targets.feature::doctor reports platform, accelerators, and SDKs separately
05_platform_and_targets.feature::doctor names the AMD device class it found
05_platform_and_targets.feature::--cross permits a target with no local device
05_platform_and_targets.feature::naming a non-native target is cross generation and says so
05_platform_and_targets.feature::-O4 is rejected under cross generation
05_platform_and_targets.feature::no vendor library is required to start the tool
05_platform_and_targets.feature::doctor distinguishes "measured" from "supported"
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::a single input profiles and then optimizes by default
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::an existing artifact is refused, and --force says that it overwrote
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::--force overwrites, and says that it did
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::-i stops after the profile
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::the default level is reproducible
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::-O4 requires a device and refuses honestly without one
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::a forced absence is applied, not merely printed
02_transform_dispatch.feature::-o wins over any extension inference
02_transform_dispatch.feature::routes are enumerable with their requirements, and asking writes nothing
02_transform_dispatch.feature::--via pins the intermediates, and a pin nothing satisfies is refused
02_transform_dispatch.feature::an unreadable input names the missing capability, never a silent no-op
02_transform_dispatch.feature::a target missing from this build fails distinguishably from one nobody wrote
02_transform_dispatch.feature::two inputs of different forms are two jobs, not a route request
03_intermediates.feature::--keep-dir implies -k and places the hops there
03_intermediates.feature::a failed hop still cleans up, and says which hop failed
03_intermediates.feature::-k preserves the intermediates of a failed run for debugging
10_portability_and_grammar.feature::verbosity is repeatable and additive
10_portability_and_grammar.feature::diagnostics never go to stdout when stdout carries a result
07_stats_and_license.feature::-s reports prior conversions relevant to the kernels in the arguments
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::a socket daemon is refused until it can authenticate its callers
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::a killed run leaves no scratch behind
01_form_detection.feature::the form table is data, so resolution is uniform across every row
06_toolchains.feature::an unpinned entry will not be downloaded at all
06_toolchains.feature::a tool with no entry for this platform is refused, not guessed at
02_transform_dispatch.feature::the fidelity class is printed on every conversion, not only with --route
07_stats_and_license.feature::the kernel identity is resolved, not string-matched on the filename
11_io_edges.feature::two concurrent runs do not corrupt the shared state directory
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::the same hazard report is produced for a tile-rs input
07_stats_and_license.feature::a corpus that fails its seal is reported, not silently ignored
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::an unmeasured architecture blocks optimization above O1
06_toolchains.feature::the daemon does not install on an agent's behalf by default
11_io_edges.feature::an interrupted run cleans up on the next run
12_run.feature::the kernel runs on this machine and matches the reference
12_run.feature::torch is consulted and the three sources are compared
10_portability_and_grammar.feature::the tool builds for every supported target triple
05_platform_and_targets.feature::the same binary reports correctly on every host it is copied to
09_ui.feature::--ui native is refused rather than silently served as a web view
02_transform_dispatch.feature::a lower is chosen when the output form sits below the input
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::-O3 asks the target's own compiler
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::-O4 records what it measured and invents nothing
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::a model that cannot be provisioned does not take the kernel tools with it
09_ui.feature::the wasm bundle is served from the same address
08_daemon_and_mcp.feature::provisioning an engine is explicit, reported, and cleaned up after
09_ui.feature::the bundle does what it claims, executed
09_ui.feature::the checked-in bundle has not drifted from its source
02_transform_dispatch.feature::an intrinsic the emitter does not understand is refused, never copied
04_profile_and_optimize.feature::-O4 verifies a width before recommending it
